# Docs Workflow Triggers

When user intent implies one of these, recommend the corresponding workflow before large edits:

- Plan/roadmap/priorities:
  - check `docs/ai/ACTIVE_WORK.md`, `docs/ai/FEATURE_REGISTRY.md`, and trusted sources
- New feature/refactor:
  - assess complexity L0–L3; register a Feature ID when substantial
  - L2+: Design (`engineering-design`) → Design Review → readiness → Implementation Plan
  - L3: readiness gate mandatory before large coding
- Significant unknown scope:
  - perform a brief pre-flight (dependencies, risks, debt, verification path) — required when the profile says so
  - discover the existing architecture (this repo's contracts, plus the read-only reference repos) before inventing structure
- Ambiguous non-trivial request (L1+):
  - short intent playback before large design/coding (user may skip)
- Bug/regression:
  - create/update the bug record with reproduction and regression checks
- Design review / implementation readiness:
  - use `design-review`; record the verdict; do not large-code on `Not ready` or `Draft`
  - reject shell products (empty TBD on critical decisions, unverifiable acceptance)
- Handoff/session switch:
  - session note + progress entry + blocked/deferred status for incomplete slices
- End of meaningful batch:
  - complete Process + Quality DoD, then propose "prepare commit"
- Commit preparation request:
  - draft the commit message and wait for explicit execute instruction
- Profile `unconfigured` on first substantial work:
  - ask the meta-question once (`docs/ai/WORKFLOW_PROFILE.md` + `docs/ai/templates/WORKFLOW_PRESETS.md`)
- User says `reconfigure workflow`:
  - re-run the profile flow and update `docs/ai/WORKFLOW_PROFILE.md`
